the logic here is a bit confusing.

on line 376 below we only set the `strict` property if `supportsStrictMode == true`
but `resolveJsonSchemaStrictSampling` can return undefined when `supportsStrictMode` is false and then we look at `defaultStrict`? not sure when we need that.

maybe something like this is clearer?

```ts
   const constrainedStrict = resolveJsonSchemaStrictSampling(tool, supportsStrictMode);

   if (supportsStrictMode) {
      functionTool.strict = constrainedStrict ?? defaultStrict;
   }
 ```

not sure if this is better.

